---
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import RemovalForm from "../components/RemovalForm.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { RELEASES, servedStableRelease } from "../lib/releases";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, EARLY_ACCESS_EMAIL, EMAIL_FROM, getPage } from "../lib/site";

const page = getPage("/privacy");
const kalvoiceShipped = servedStableRelease(RELEASES) !== null;
// Owner-approved 2026-09-30 (target/recovery-B10-release/CHECKOUT-GO-LIVE.md): shown only when the
// site is built with paid checkout open (docs/BILLING.md §9); closed, the notice is unchanged.
const checkoutOpen = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CHECKOUT_ENABLED === "true";
const hours = EARLY_ACCESS_EMAIL.linkTtlHours;
const sender = EMAIL_FROM.replace(/^.*<|>$/g, "");
---
<Base title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <PageHead
    title="Privacy"
    lead="What kalcoded.com and KalCode accounts collect, what we use it for, and how to remove it."
  >
    <p class="muted small">Last updated October 5, 2026</p>
  </PageHead>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What we store for early access</h2>
      <p>When you join early access, we store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your email address,</li>
        <li>the date and time you joined,</li>
        <li>the page you joined from (for example, <code>/download</code>),</li>
        <li>the version of the consent text shown next to the form,</li>
        <li>whether you have confirmed your address, and when,</li>
        <li>
          when we last emailed you and how many emails we sent that day, so nobody can use the form
          to flood your inbox,
        </li>
        <li>
          for each confirmation or removal link we email you, a one-way fingerprint of the link (never
          the link itself) and when it expires.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That is all for early access. We do not store your IP address, your browser's user agent, or
        any other information about your device.
      </p>

      <h2>What we use it for</h2>
      <p>
        We use your early-access email address only to contact you about KalCode early access and launch. We do
        not sell it, share it for marketing, or add it to anyone else's list.
      </p>

      <h2 id="confirm">Confirming your address</h2>
      <p>
        When you join, we email you a link to confirm your address, from <code>{sender}</code>.
        You are on the list only once you open the link and press <strong>Confirm my email</strong>.
        Opening the link on its own changes nothing, so mail scanners that open links cannot confirm
        for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links work once and expire after {hours} hours. A sign-up that is not confirmed in that time
        is deleted automatically, together with its links. The form can't check who owns an address,
        so if you get a confirmation email you didn't expect, ignore it and the address is deleted.
        The form shows the same message whether or not an address is already on the list, and we
        send at most one email to an address every {EARLY_ACCESS_EMAIL.minIntervalMinutes} minutes
        and {EARLY_ACCESS_EMAIL.dailyPerAddress} a day.
      </p>
      <p>
        Addresses that joined before we started confirming (September 2026) are kept as unconfirmed
        and are not emailed automatically. We will ask each of them once to confirm; an address
        that doesn't confirm within {hours} hours of that request is deleted.
      </p>
      <p>
        Replies to our emails go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We
        use no open or click tracking: the emails contain no images or tracking pixels, and every
        link goes straight to kalcoded.com.
      </p>
      <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
      <p>
        The list is stored in a Cloudflare D1 database operated for kalcoded.com. We keep your
        address until you remove it or until we close the early-access list, whichever comes first.
      </p>
      <p>
        Removing your address deletes it from the list permanently, together with any links we sent
        you. Cloudflare keeps
        point-in-time recovery copies of D1 databases for up to 30 days, so a removed address
        can remain in those copies until they expire.
      </p>

      <h2 id="accounts">KalCode accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You can create a KalCode account on this site or in the KalCode app by signing in with Google,
        Microsoft or a one-time email link. For your account, we store:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>your email address, verified by the email link or by Google or Microsoft, and when it was verified,</li>
        <li>
          if you sign in with Google or Microsoft, that service's identifier for your account (from
          Google or Microsoft we keep only this identifier and your email address),
        </li>
        <li>the display name you choose, if you set one,</li>
        <li>when you created the account and when you chose a plan,</li>
        <li>your plan, how it was granted and, for a paid plan, its billing period, with a record of every change to it,</li>
        <li>
          for each signed-in session on this site or in the app, a one-way fingerprint of its sign-in
          token (never the token itself), whether it is a website or app session, and when it was
          created and expires,
        </li>
        <li>
          for each KalVoice Request counted against your plan, a random request ID and the time it was
          recorded, never audio, transcripts or what you asked.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We use this to sign you in, keep your plan and KalVoice Request allowance the same on this site
        and in the app, and send the sign-in and deletion links you ask for. Those links are the only
        emails your account gets from us, and they expire after 10 minutes. To stop abuse, sign-in and
        account emails are limited per network, per address and per account, using short-lived
        counters stored under keyed one-way fingerprints of your IP address and email address, never
        the addresses themselves. We keep a record of each account email we send (its purpose, the day
        and those fingerprints, never your address) for 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the KalCode app, your session stays in your operating system's credential store. While you
        are signed in, the app contacts api.kalcoded.com to load your account, plan and KalVoice usage
        and to count KalVoice Requests. The app never sends us your prompts, transcripts, code or
        workspace content.
      </p>
      <p>
        Account data is stored in a Cloudflare D1 database operated for api.kalcoded.com, and account
        emails are delivered by Resend, as described below.
      </p>{checkoutOpen && <p>Payments are processed by Stripe on its own hosted pages. When you start a checkout, we give Stripe your account email address and account ID; we keep your Stripe customer and subscription IDs, plan, subscription status and billing period, never your card details. Deleting your KalCode account does not delete your records at Stripe, which keeps them under its own privacy policy.</p>}

      <h2 id="delete-account">Deleting your account</h2>
      <p>
        Sign in on the <a href="/account">account page</a> and press <strong>Delete account</strong>.
        We email you a one-time link that expires after 10 minutes; open it in the browser where you
        are signed in to confirm. You can't delete an account while a paid subscription has not ended
        or a checkout is in progress, so cancel the subscription and wait for its paid period to end
        first.
      </p>
      <p>
        Deleting your account replaces your email address with a placeholder, removes your display
        name and signs out every session on this site and in the app. We keep the rest of the
        account record, including its internal ID, its plan and billing history and its KalVoice
        Request counts, so those records stay complete. A Google or Microsoft identifier stays linked
        to the deleted account until you next sign in with that Google or Microsoft account, which
        releases it. Cloudflare's point-in-time recovery copies of the database can keep the
        previous data for up to 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Your voice and KalVoice</h2>
      <p>
        This site never uses your microphone. In the KalCode app,
        {kalvoiceShipped ? "KalVoice" : "KalVoice (in development)"} transcribes dictation on your
        device. Voice audio is held in memory only while it is transcribed, then discarded. It is not
        retained, not uploaded, and never reaches us or this site. The app downloads its default speech
        model from kalcoded.com by itself, and if you remove the model, the app doesn't download it
        again on its own. Once speech is ready, KalCode also downloads its on-device interpreter
        (about 850 MB) from the same signed catalog. Turn off Prepare local intelligence
        automatically in Settings › KalVoice to download it yourself instead. These downloads send no
        audio or text.
      </p>
      <p>
        KalVoice interprets commands on your device. It never uses the AI providers you connected, or
        KalCode's servers, to understand what you said. Words you dictate into a coding agent (Claude
        Code, Codex, Cursor or Gemini CLI), and coding tasks you send to it, go to that provider under
        your own account and that provider's terms, exactly as if you typed them yourself.
      </p>

      <h2 id="email-delivery">Resend delivers our emails</h2>
      <p>
        We send early-access confirmation and removal emails, and KalCode account sign-in and
        deletion emails, through Resend (resend.com), our email-delivery processor. For each email, Resend receives your email address and the message we send you,
        including its link, and processes them only to deliver that email, under its own privacy
        policy and data processing terms. Resend keeps a record of each email it sends, including the
        address and the message, for a limited time under its own retention policy. The links in
        those messages stop working once used, or after {hours} hours (early access) or 10 minutes
        (account emails). We send no other emails through Resend and share nothing else with it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cloudflare as our infrastructure provider</h2>
      <p>
        kalcoded.com and the account service at api.kalcoded.com run on Cloudflare. Like any network
        provider, Cloudflare processes technical request data — such as your IP address — to deliver
        pages and protect the site from abuse,
        under its own privacy policy. To stop automated abuse, the early-access forms and email
        links count requests per IP address using Cloudflare's rate limiting; that short-lived
        counter is not stored by us. Our own server logs record only events and errors (for example,
        "confirmation email sent") and never contain email addresses, links or IP addresses.
      </p>

      <h2>No analytics, no tracking cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no analytics, no tracking pixels, no advertising, and no third-party scripts.
        The only cookie we set keeps you signed in to your KalCode account: when you sign in on this
        site, api.kalcoded.com sets a strictly necessary, HttpOnly session cookie that expires after
        30 days and is removed when you sign out or delete your account. Cloudflare may set a
        strictly necessary security cookie if its bot protection is triggered for a request.
      </p>
      <p>
        To know how KalCode is distributed, our server counts the files it serves: installer
        downloads, and the KalCode app's update checks and update downloads. Each count records only
        the time, the kind of request, the platform and architecture of the file, and the KalCode
        version involved. We do not record your IP address, browser details, a device or
        installation identifier, or anything else that could identify you, and the KalCode app sends
        no telemetry.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose a light or dark theme, that choice is saved in your browser's local storage
        and never sent to us. If you pick a plan on the pricing page, the account page keeps that
        choice in local storage so it survives signing in; it expires after an hour. While a Google
        or Microsoft sign-in is in progress, its one-time security values are kept in that browser
        tab's session storage and removed when you return.
      </p>

      <h2 id="remove">Remove your email</h2>
      <p>
        Enter the address you used. If it is on the early-access list, we email it a link; open the
        link and press <strong>Remove my email</strong> to delete the address permanently. The link
        works once and expires after {hours} hours. So that nobody can find out who is on the list,
        the message on this page is the same whether or not the address was on it. Every
        confirmation email also contains a removal link.
      </p>
      <RemovalForm />

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        kalcoded.com is run by the KalCode team. For privacy questions or requests, including
        asking what we hold about you, email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If what we collect changes, we will update this notice before the change takes effect and change the date at the top of the
        page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
